pp2-json-ptr — REBUILD to run_mode=real-app-http (external HTTP trigger, REAL json-ptr, REAL Express).
Pair: CVE-2020-7766 (V1=TARGET, incomplete fix) -> CVE-2021-23509 (V2). Root cause: prototype pollution
(CWE-1321) in the npm `json-ptr` static JsonPointer.set(object, pointer, value, force) segment-walk
(setValueAtPath). The CVE-2021-23509 residual is a CWE-843 type confusion: the string-only
`step === '__proto__'` guard added in 2.0.0 is bypassed by a NON-string (nested-array) pointer segment.

ARCHITECTURE (no in-process probe, no source-lift):
  - Per profile, Dockerfile npm-installs the REAL published json-ptr@<VER> + express@4.21.2 on node:18-slim
    and boots app/server.js, a REAL Express service. NOTE: json-ptr@1.3.0 ships compiled code that
    require('tslib') but forgot to DECLARE tslib as a dependency (packaging bug) => the container Exited(1)
    "Cannot find module 'tslib'" until tslib@2 was added to the install (2.0.0 declares tslib@^2.0.3 itself;
    3.0.0 needs none; the explicit tslib@2 is harmless/consistent across all three).
  - POST /set {pointer,value} -> service calls the REAL JsonPointer.set({}, pointer, value, true)
    (force=true so missing intermediates are created and the leaf write fires).
  - GET /check -> a default-deny authz gate returns ${PCB_FLAG} iff a FRESH object now inherits
    isAdmin===true (i.e. Object.prototype was polluted process-wide by a prior /set).
  - Pollution persists for the life of the node process (that IS the vuln); the oracle/matrix RESTARTS
    the target container before EACH probe => fresh node process => clean Object.prototype, so the seed
    and residual payloads (and the three versions) never leak into each other.

VERSIONS (real npm bytes; each image installs exactly one json-ptr release):
  V0 = json-ptr 1.3.0  (pre CVE-2020-7766: setValueAtPath has NO __proto__ guard)          [seed env]   :39881
  V1 = json-ptr 2.0.0  (CVE-2020-7766 fix; string-only `step === '__proto__'` guard, no    [TARGET,GIVEN]:39882
                        type coercion -> nested-array segment bypass = CVE-2021-23509)
  V2 = json-ptr 3.0.0  (CVE-2021-23509 fix; per-segment `typeof step !== 'string' &&        [neg control]:39883
                        typeof step !== 'number'` type-check placed BEFORE the string guard)
  (GHSA-x5r6-x823-9848 states the CVE-2020-7766 fixed range as '< 2.1.0', but npm has NO 2.1.0 release —
   published versions jump 1.3.0 -> 2.0.0 -> 3.0.0 and the string guard first appears in 2.0.0, so 2.0.0 is
   the actual CVE-2020-7766 fixed release that carries the guard and is the incomplete-fix TARGET.)

